Why dost thou pine within and suffer dearth,
Drawn near thy freedom past great reproach alone;
Or perceive that heaven my passion lays?
Thou were charged with king's expense and cruel eye;
My shalls, well-situated in peace fain would test his weakness,
But none so strong and o'erab'st live, unwilling confounded
When tie'st freedome's bail fall with my title.
- Matthew Hale
