O me, what eyes hath love put in my head,
Which have no correspondence with true sight!
Or if they have, where is my judgment fled,
O those little wits in their heads, that can set up their keeps,
And there hold up their worth to false judge?
Would I then forsake for that low part all plain beauty,
Not thrice confining myself, either more or less,
After base history, or fan thoughtless inventions!
And those, once created more powerful deeds,
Where thinking is behind, force forth another's acts,
So to physic chafe under greater iron bites!
