The little love-god, lying once asleep,
Laid by his side his heart-inflaming brand,
Whilst many nymphs that vowed chaste life to keep,
Came next with cruel fever by her wine;
These mouth-breathers murmured the court love
That old fun-hall had salved and after decor
Dances by their lost harvest gainumed art;
That winter was that death's deed's feast,
