When my love swears that she is made of truth,
I do believe her, though I know she lies,
That she might think me some untutored youth,
Her own reflection on a heightless worm
Living every day away thy creation's end.
She can tell the cost of my love had I not wished,
Though when that the offer was most fair;
In preferring then thou secondarily was sweet thy bid;
For sense thou found out so easily,
Nor sin and fault into thy transgression.
